{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":70253847,"ns":0,"title":"Bekić's theorem","extract":"In computability theory, Bekić's theorem or Bekić's lemma is a theorem about fixed-points which allows splitting a mutual recursion into recursions on one variable at a time. It was created by Austrian Hans Bekić (1936-1982) in 1969, and published posthumously in a book by Cliff Jones in 1984.","description":"Theorem about fixed points of multiple variables","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}